+    "body": "## Problem\n\n`/task --ci-cd https://github.com/link-assistant/agent` created\n[link-assistant/agent#287](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/287), whose\n\"Recent CI/CD runs on `main`\" table has **20 rows for only 2 workflows** — the same\n*JS CI/CD Pipeline* (14 rows) and *Rust CI/CD Pipeline* (6 rows) repeated for commits\nspanning 2026-04-25 … 2026-07-30 — and a summary of \"CI/CD runs found: 20 (9 not passing)\"\nthat counts months-old failures as current.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`/fix --ci-cd` and `/task --ci-cd` share `prepareCiCdIssue()`. It lists the runs of the\nlatest default-branch commit; when that commit produced none — verified for `agent`'s\n`fd42c4b` (\"0.25.4\"): `actions/runs?head_sha=fd42c4b…` returns `total_count: 0` — it falls\nback to `actions/runs?branch=main`, which returns runs **across many commits**.\n`buildRunsSection()` mapped that array 1:1 to table rows, and `summarizeRunFailures()`\ncounted it raw. `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs` has no \"latest run per workflow\"\noption, so the collapse has to happen client-side — and nothing did it.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `runWorkflowKey()` — workflow identity: `workflow_id`, then `path`, then `name`; a run\n  with no identifying field is never treated as a duplicate.\n- `dedupeRunsByWorkflow()` — keeps the most recent run per workflow (`created_at`, then\n  `run_attempt`, then `id`), preserving input order. `countDuplicateRuns()` reports how\n  many rows it drops.\n- `buildRunsSection()` deduplicates and gained `includeCommit`, so the branch-fallback\n  table shows which commit each surviving run belongs to.\n- `summarizeRunFailures()` / `buildCiCdIssueBody()` count the deduplicated set, so the\n  table and the \"CI/CD runs found\" line always agree.\n- The runs query now selects `workflow_id`, `path`, `created_at`, `run_attempt`, and the\n  fallback fetches `per_page=100` instead of `20` — after collapsing, a workflow whose last\n  run is older than the 20 most recent would otherwise disappear entirely.\n- `prepareCiCdIssue()` returns `fetchedRuns`/`duplicateRuns` and logs\n  `ℹ️ Collapsed N older CI/CD run(s) …`, which `/fix` prints.\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\nRegenerating the issue body from the *exact* 20 runs behind agent#287\n(`docs/case-studies/issue-2125/data/`) now yields:\n\n```\n| Workflow | Status | Conclusion | Commit | Run |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| JS CI/CD Pipeline | completed | failure | `cff4148` | [run](.../30572373896) |\n| Rust CI/CD Pipeline | completed | failure | `7af549d` | [run](.../28688932169) |\n```\n\nwith `CI/CD runs found: 2 (2 not passing)`. Full \"before\" payload, the regenerated body and\nthe analysis are in [`docs/case-studies/issue-2125`](docs/case-studies/issue-2125/README.md).\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test-fix-ci-cd.mjs` (suite `default`) gains four regression tests, including an\nend-to-end `prepareCiCdIssue()` run through a stubbed `gh` that reproduces the release-commit\n→ branch-fallback → duplicate-row path and asserts the stale run is gone, the count is not\ninflated, and the verbose collapse line is emitted.\n\nFixes #2125\n",
