+  {
+    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements `/fix --ci-cd <repository>` (issue #1733): a command that **automatically generates and solves a CI/CD remediation issue** for a target repository, from the CLI or from Telegram.\n\nGiven a repository, `/fix --ci-cd`:\n\n1. **Detects languages** via the GitHub `/languages` API and selects the matching CI/CD templates, **ordered by detected language** (byte-weighted; JavaScript + TypeScript merge into one template).\n2. **Inspects the latest default-branch commit** and lists its CI/CD runs in the issue. Release/tag commits frequently have no runs of their own, so it **falls back to the most recent default-branch runs** (clearly relabelled \"Recent CI/CD runs on `<branch>`\").\n3. **Creates the remediation issue**, reusing the title and description of [web-capture#139](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/issues/139) **exactly, minus the parts `--development-log` and `--deep-analysis` already provide**, and linking to `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`.\n4. **Hands the issue off to `/solve --development-log --deep-analysis --auto-merge`**, forwarding every option `/fix` does not consume itself (e.g. `--tool`, `--model`, `--think`).\n5. Supports `--dry-run` (preview the issue) and `--no-solve` (create only).\n\n## How the \"exact title and description, minus what the options provide\" rule works\n\nThe upstream case-study paragraph is **retired and never represented in the generated prompt**. `--development-log` is its sole replacement and collects under `./dev/log/issues/{id}/pulls/{pr}`; no option combination, including `--no-solve` or a partial option set, restores the old folder convention. The remaining conditional paragraphs carry `providedBy`, the `/solve` option that injects their equivalent instruction:\n\n| Paragraph | `providedBy` | Dropped when |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Compile data / retired case study | — | always excluded; replaced by `--development-log` |\n| Provide debug output | `--deep-analysis` | `--deep-analysis` is passed |\n| Report upstream template issues | `--deep-analysis` | `--deep-analysis` is passed |\n| Compare full file tree / best-practices link / keep-working | — | never |\n\nThe behavior is derived from reading `buildDeepAnalysisPrompt` and `buildDevelopmentLogPrompt` rather than guessed. Two details matter:\n\n- **The issue is created as type `Bug`** (with the `bug` label). `buildDeepAnalysisPrompt` only emits the root-cause / debug-output / report-upstream instructions for Bug-typed issues, so the Bug type is what makes dropping those paragraphs valid. Issue types are org-scoped and labels are repo-scoped, so both are best-effort: creation retries without the metadata rather than aborting.\n- **There is no legacy fallback.** Review feedback clarified that the upstream case-study paragraph conflicts with `--development-log`; it was removed as a constant and paragraph entry, rather than merely hidden by the default option set. Regression tests cover default, no-options, development-log-only, and deep-analysis-only prompt construction.\n\n## Requirements coverage (issue #1733)\n\n| Requirement | Status |\n| --- | --- |\n| New `/fix --ci-cd` command | ✅ `src/fix.mjs` + `package.json` bin |\n| Check latest default-branch commit + list its CI/CD runs | ✅ with branch fallback |\n| Use web-capture#139 title **exactly** (as re-titled upstream) | ✅ `CI_CD_ISSUE_TITLE`, pinned by a test |\n| Use the description exactly, **omitting** parts `--development-log`/`--deep-analysis` provide | ✅ retired paragraph structurally absent; deep-analysis paragraphs use `providedBy` filtering |\n| Template links sorted by detected languages | ✅ `mapLanguagesToTemplates` |\n| Detect languages used in the repository | ✅ `gh api .../languages` |\n| Behave like `/solve --development-log --deep-analysis --auto-merge` | ✅ `buildSolveArgs` (each flag deduped) |\n| Pass through `--tool`/`--model`/`--think` (and every other non-fix option) | ✅ `partitionFixArgs` |\n| Link to `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` in the issue | ✅ |\n| `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` updated in all languages (en/zh/hi/ru) | ✅ |\n| Add PHP template to the list | ✅ `link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` |\n| Compile data + deep case study to `docs/case-studies/issue-1733/` | ✅ re-done against the updated description |\n| Apply the change everywhere it belongs (whole-repo scope, per review) | ✅ Telegram `/fix`, `--fix`/`TELEGRAM_FIX`, help text + docs in 4 locales |\n\n## Architecture\n\n- **`src/fix.ci-cd.lib.mjs`** — pure, network-free core (template mapping, language normalization, tagged-paragraph issue-body building, arg partitioning). Deliberately avoids importing `github.lib.mjs` (whose transitive chain performs a top-level network fetch) so unit tests run fast and offline.\n- **`src/fix.mjs`** — thin CLI that talks to `gh`, creates the issue via the existing `/task` `createTaskIssue` helper, and spawns `solve.mjs`.\n- **`src/telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs`** — the in-chat `/fix` handler, mirroring `telegram-task-command.lib.mjs`: implies `--ci-cd`, normalizes `owner/repo` to a full URL, forwards the chat locale as `--language`, validates model/isolation, and ignores forwarded/replied commands (#1922). Toggle with `--no-fix` / `TELEGRAM_FIX=false`.\n- **`src/telegram.config.lib.mjs`** — the bot's yargs option surface, extracted from `telegram-bot.mjs` (adding `--fix` pushed it past the repo's 1500-line `max-lines` cap). Mirrors the existing `solve.config.lib.mjs` / `hive.config.lib.mjs` / `task.config.lib.mjs` pattern, and makes the option surface testable without starting a bot.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- `docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` (+ `.zh`, `.hi`, `.ru`): PHP template rows (templates, formatting/PHP CS Fixer, static analysis/PHPStan, changeset/changelog.d) and a new **Automatic CI/CD Remediation** section with the language → template mapping.\n- `README.md` (+ `.zh`, `.hi`, `.ru`): new `/fix - Auto-Remediate CI/CD` command section.\n- `docs/CONFIGURATION.md` (+ 3 locales): the `TELEGRAM_FIX` toggle.\n- `src/locales/{en,hi,ru,zh}.lino`: `/fix` help text.\n- `docs/case-studies/issue-1733/`: deep analysis (requirements R1–R25, solution plans, reused-components map), captured data (`data/`), and `research-sources.json`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test-fix-ci-cd.mjs` — **27 tests.** PHP template, repo parsing, language normalization/sorting, JS+TS merge, unmatched languages, template-section priority + fallback, run summarization, run-table rendering, issue title/body sections + sorting, branch-fallback heading, **the paragraph-omission matrix plus a structural no-fallback assertion**, arg partitioning, and solve-arg assembly.\n- `tests/test-telegram-fix-command.mjs` — **22 tests.** Command recognition, `--ci-cd` implied and not duplicated, option preservation, shorthand normalization, missing repo, non-GitHub URL rejection, spawn args/tool/isolation/urlContext, locale forwarding, invalid isolation/model, forwarded-or-reply ignored, disabled instance, stopped chat, non-group, unauthorized topic, old message, and regex registration.\n- `tests/test-telegram-config.mjs` — **6 tests.** Every command enabled by default, `--no-fix`, `TELEGRAM_FIX=false`/`true`, `--fix` overriding the env, strict-mode rejection, isolation default.\n\nAll three are in the default suite. `npm run lint` and `npm run format:check` are clean.\n\n## How to reproduce / try\n\n```bash\n# Preview without creating anything:\nfix link-assistant/hive-mind --ci-cd --dry-run\n\n# Create the issue but do not start /solve:\nfix link-assistant/hive-mind --ci-cd --no-solve\n\n# Full flow, forwarding solve options:\nfix link-assistant/hive-mind --ci-cd --tool codex --model gpt-5.5 --think max\n```\n\nFrom Telegram (`--ci-cd` is implied):\n\n```\n/fix https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind --model sonnet\n```\n\nCloses #1733.\n",
