+  { "body": "## Summary\n\nThis pull request implements a solution for #2082: Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all\n\n### Changes\n- 68 file(s) modified\n- 116881 line(s) added\n- 335 line(s) removed\n\n### Issue Reference\nFixes #2082\n\n---\n*This PR was created automatically by the AI issue solver*", "mergedAt": "2026-07-19T16:11:18Z", "number": 2083, "title": "'Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all'", "url": "https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2083" },
+  {
+    "body": "## Problem\n\nA `fix` run ended with a Telegram notification saying only `Work session failed (exit code: 1)`. Its wrapper log ([raw logs](https://github.com/konard/private-logs/tree/main/log-tmp-start-command-logs-isolation-docker-2757eeb3-68e6-43bb-8a6a-20c55dfd2958)) is **286,452,210 bytes / 1,354,860 lines** and ends in a V8 heap abort:\n\n```text\nFATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory\n❌ Error: solve exited with code null\nReason: exitCode=1 oomKilled=false\n```\n\nThe log was large because hive-mind wrote its own output into it, repeatedly. `getPullRequestChangeStats()` ran `gh pr diff` with `command-stream`'s default `mirror: true`, so the whole diff was echoed to stdout, copied into the session log by the stdio interceptor (#1549), published by `--attach-logs` and committed into the branch by `--development-log` — so the *next* `gh pr diff` contained the previous log. The development-log slice committed per iteration went 2.7 MB → 38 MB → 80 MB → 199 MB.\n\n## How to reproduce\n\nRun `solve`/`fix` with `--attach-logs --development-log` on a pull request whose branch already carries a committed session log: each iteration mirrors the whole diff into the log, and the log is committed again. `docs/case-studies/issue-2135/scripts/measure-session-log.mjs <log>` reproduces every number quoted in the case study from the raw log.\n\n## Root causes and fixes\n\n| # | Root cause | Fix |\n| - | ---------- | --- |\n| RC1 | `gh pr diff` probed with default mirroring, so the diff entered the session log | `src/pull-request-changes.lib.mjs` probes quietly and warns past 8 MB |\n| RC2 | The same loud-probe pattern in 12 other modules; `contributing-guidelines` also called `.raw()` on the retry-wrapped `$`, a `TypeError` that silently disabled guideline detection | quiet-probe sweep over 13 modules; `.raw()` removed |\n| RC3 | `measureDiff` kept several whole-diff copies plus one match array entry per added line | single streaming pass, returning `diffBytes` |\n| RC4 | V8 `abort()` → `SIGABRT` → `code === null`; `hive` computed `code \\|\\| 0`, recording an OOM-killed worker as a **success** | new `src/child-exit.lib.mjs`, used by all seven spawners |\n| RC5 | The log grew 19 MB → 199 MB without a word | new `src/log-growth.lib.mjs`: warnings at 64 MB / 256 MB / 1 GB |\n| RC6 | A failed development-log publication left its copies untracked; watch mode read them as the AI's uncommitted work and restarted the session with instructions to commit them | `discardUnpublishedDevelopmentLog()` cleans up on every publication failure path |\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test-issue-2135-log-explosion.mjs` — 32 tests in the `default` suite:\n\n- the diff probe is called with `mirror: false, capture: true` and prints nothing (verified with a `$` double that records its options);\n- a synthetic 9 MB diff is measured correctly, reports `diffBytes` and produces a warning naming the usual cause;\n- source sweeps assert all 13 probes stay quiet, that `contributing-guidelines` never calls `.raw()`, and that all 7 spawner modules describe how their child ended instead of interpolating a null code;\n- `attachChildExitHandlers` maps `close(null, 'SIGABRT')` to exit 1 with one error log, and passes ordinary exits through unchanged;\n- the growth tracker warns once per threshold and resets with the log file;\n- a development-log publication that cannot stage, inspect or commit removes what it wrote, while a successful one keeps its artifacts.\n\nFull `default` suite and `npm run lint` / `npm run format:check` pass locally.\n\n## Case study\n\n`docs/case-studies/issue-2135/` holds the deep analysis required by the issue: the requirement inventory, the line-numbered timeline (16:52:17 → 18:26:42), the amplification table, RC1–RC6, the solution plan, prior art (`command-stream` mirror/capture, Node `maxBuffer`, `execa`, `gh pr diff --name-only`, log rotation, `--max-old-space-size` — and why the last two were rejected), and bounded raw excerpts with SHA-256 checksums. The 286 MB log itself is deliberately not committed; the measuring script regenerates its metrics.\n\nThe issue also asks whether this belongs in another project: it does not. Every link in the chain is hive-mind's own code.\n\nFixes #2135\n",
