+    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #2128.\n\n- replace the unsafe workflow-level concurrency example with job-level patterns for cancellable read-only checks and protected repository-wide writers\n- document dependency cancellation, matrix grouping, cross-workflow writer serialization, pending-job replacement, `queue: max`, and `!cancelled()` propagation\n- keep the English, Hindi, Russian, and Chinese CI/CD guides synchronized\n- add default-suite regression coverage that rejects the main-cancelling expression and requires the safe check/writer patterns in every translation\n\n## Reproduction\n\nBefore this change, `node tests/cicd-best-practices-concurrency-2128.test.mjs` failed because every guide contained `cancel-in-progress` with `github.ref == refs/heads/main`, allowing an in-flight main release to be cancelled.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `node tests/cicd-best-practices-concurrency-2128.test.mjs`\n- [x] `npm test` (all 370 default test files)\n- [x] `npm run lint`\n- [x] `npm run format:check`\n- [x] `git diff --check`\n- [x] verified the branch contains the latest `origin/main`\n",
