+    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #2085.\n\n`/fix --ci-cd` **does** call the real `/solve` in a real working session — this\nis proven by the captured solve-session metadata of the run cited in the issue,\nPR #2083, whose `rawCommand` is a genuine `node .../src/solve.mjs …` invocation.\nThe actual defect is narrower: the Telegram bot's **operator solve overrides**\n(`TELEGRAM_SOLVE_OVERRIDES`, e.g. `--attach-logs`) were merged into `/solve` and\n`/hive` but **never into `/fix`**. So the solve launched by `/fix` ran without\nthe operator's configured defaults — exactly the \"`--attach-logs` were not\napplied\" symptom.\n\nPer #1733, `/fix` should behave as a straightforward combination of `/task` +\n`/solve`. This PR makes `/fix` reuse the **identical** override mechanism\n`/solve` already uses — no new/fancy machinery.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`mergeArgsWithOverrides()` lived inside `telegram-bot.mjs` and was only applied\nby the `/solve` and `/hive` handlers. The `/fix` handler\n(`telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs`) never received `solveOverrides`, so the\noverrides were absent from the args forwarded to `solve.mjs`. The override must\nbe baked into the **arguments** (not read from env by `fix.mjs`) because Docker\nisolation only forwards explicitly-listed `-e` env vars into the container, so a\nDocker `/fix` session would never see `TELEGRAM_SOLVE_OVERRIDES`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/args-overrides.lib.mjs`** (new): shared `mergeArgsWithOverrides`\n  extracted from `telegram-bot.mjs` (adds `Array.isArray` null-safety) so\n  `/solve`, `/hive` and `/fix` share one implementation without a circular\n  import on the bot entry point.\n- **`src/telegram-bot.mjs`**: import the shared helper; pass `solveOverrides`\n  into `registerFixCommand`.\n- **`src/telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs`**: merge `solveOverrides` into the fix\n  args (overrides win, appended last for yargs' last-wins parsing), honor an\n  optional `--isolation` override from the overrides, validate the model on the\n  merged args, and surface a `🔒 Solve overrides: …` line in the work-session\n  info block.\n- **Tests**: `tests/test-args-overrides.mjs` (new unit tests for the real\n  helper) and new `/fix` override cases in `tests/test-telegram-fix-command.mjs`.\n- **Case study**: `docs/case-studies/issue-2085/` — timeline, requirements,\n  root-cause analysis, solution, codebase audit, and existing-components review,\n  with primary evidence (`data/pr-2083-solve-metadata.json`).\n- **Changeset**: patch bump.\n\n## How to reproduce (before the fix)\n\n1. Run the Telegram bot with `TELEGRAM_SOLVE_OVERRIDES=\"(\\n  --attach-logs\\n)\"`.\n2. Trigger `/fix <repo>`; it generates the CI/CD issue and starts `/solve`.\n3. Inspect the started solve's `rawCommand` (session `metadata.json`): it lacks\n   `--attach-logs` (see PR #2083's captured metadata). After this fix, the\n   override is present.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/test-args-overrides.mjs` — 8/8 pass.\n- `tests/test-telegram-fix-command.mjs` — 28/28 pass (7 new override cases).\n- `tests/test-issue-1228-options-deduplication.mjs` — 19/19 pass (no regression\n  in existing override behaviour).\n",
