+    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #1952. Two distinct bugs surfaced by [xlabtg/teleton-agent PR #670](https://github.com/xlabtg/teleton-agent/pull/670):\n\n1. **Timeout-cancelled CI was misclassified as \"requires review\".** A job that hits its `timeout-minutes` limit surfaces as a **check-run** with conclusion `cancelled`, but the **parent workflow run** concludes `failure`. `getDetailedCIStatus` inspects check-runs only, so the auto-merge loop saw the lone `cancelled` check, posted a **\"Cancelled CI/CD Requires Review\"** comment, and stopped — even though the workflow run had failed and *other jobs in it had also failed*.\n2. **The session finished with no log attached despite `--attach-logs`.** Every log-attachment path in `solve.mjs` is conditional, and the stop-for-human-review exits can `return` before any iteration uploads a log.\n\n## Root cause\n\nGitHub reports a timed-out job at two levels with different conclusions:\n\n| Inspect… | Timeout looks like… | Manual cancel looks like… |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| check-runs only (old behaviour) | `cancelled` ❌ | `cancelled` |\n| workflow runs (the fix) | `failure` ✅ | `cancelled` |\n\nThe real teleton run `27821270533` concluded `failure` with jobs `Build (Runtime) (22)`, `Deploy artifacts`, `OpenAPI` all **failed** plus `Build (Runtime) (20)` **cancelled** (timeout) — yet the tool stopped for review. Full evidence and analysis: [`docs/case-studies/issue-1952/`](./docs/case-studies/issue-1952/README.md).\n\n## Changes\n\n### R1 + R2 — classify cancelled CI by workflow-run conclusions\n- New pure helper `classifyCancelledCIByWorkflowRuns` + `FAILURE_LIKE_WORKFLOW_RUN_CONCLUSIONS` (`failure`, `timed_out`, `startup_failure`) in `src/cancelled-ci-rerun.lib.mjs`.\n- `getMergeBlockers` (`src/solve.auto-merge-helpers.lib.mjs`) cancelled branch now fetches the workflow runs for the SHA and classifies:\n  - **pending** (any run not yet terminal) → `ci_pending` → keep waiting until *all* checks are terminal (R2).\n  - **failure** (any completed failure-like run) → `ci_failure` → restart the AI to fix it (R1; R2 coexisting failures).\n  - **cancelled** → original re-triggerable flow (genuine manual cancellation).\n- `src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs`: the \"Cancelled CI/CD Requires Review\" stop path is skipped when a `ci_failure` blocker coexists.\n- `src/github-merge-ci.lib.mjs`: `startup_failure` now counts as a failing run (applied codebase-wide, R7).\n\n### R3 — guarantee a log is always attached\n- `attachLogToGitHub` (`src/github.lib.mjs`) sets `global.logAttachedToGitHub = true` on **every** successful upload (both upload branches).\n- New `attachFinalLogIfMissing` (`src/attach-logs-guarantee.lib.mjs`) runs as the last step of `solve.mjs`: attaches the cumulative session log when `--attach-logs` is on, a PR exists, and nothing attached yet, then reconciles `logsAttached` so `endWorkSession` does not double-post.\n\n### R4/R5/R6\n- `docs/case-studies/issue-1952/` — downloaded evidence + deep analysis (timeline, requirements R1–R8, root causes, existing-component review). Verbose logging added in the cancelled branch (off by default). No third-party repo bug to report — the behaviour was entirely in hive-mind's own logic; GitHub Actions behaves as documented.\n\n## How to reproduce (before the fix)\nA PR whose CI workflow run concludes `failure` while one of its jobs is `cancelled` by `timeout-minutes`: the old code posted \"Cancelled CI/CD Requires Review\" and stopped instead of restarting the AI, and finished the session with no attached log.\n\n## Tests\n- `tests/test-cancelled-timeout-fail-1952.mjs` — 13 tests. Reproduces the teleton case (workflow-run `failure` + cancelled check → `failure`) and covers `timed_out`/`startup_failure`/manual-cancel/`stale`/mixed/in-progress/queued/empty + wiring.\n- `tests/test-attach-logs-safety-net-1952.mjs` — 9 tests. Global flag set only on real uploads; `attachFinalLogIfMissing` disabled / no-PR / already-attached / fires-as-last-resort; solve.mjs wiring.\n\nBoth pass locally; the changeset bumps `@link-assistant/hive-mind` (patch).\n",
+    "mergedAt": "2026-06-19T18:22:14Z",
+    "number": 1953,
+    "title": "fix(auto-merge): treat timeout-cancelled CI as failure; always attach logs (#1952)",
