+    "body": "## Summary\n\n`.jscpd.json` in this template sets `\"format\": \"console\"`. In jscpd, `format` is the list of **languages/formats to analyze**, not the output format — output is controlled by `reporters` (which this file already sets correctly).\n\nBecause `console` is not a source language, jscpd matches **zero files** and always reports `Found 0 clones.` The duplication gate is therefore a permanent false positive: it can never fail, no matter how much duplicated code a repository contains.\n\nFound while working on [link-foundation/start#158](https://github.com/link-foundation/start/issues/158) (\"check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD\").\n\n## Reproducible example\n\nTwo deliberately identical files plus this template's `format` setting:\n\n```bash\nmkdir jscpd-repro && cd jscpd-repro\nprintf 'function a(){\\n  const x=1;\\n  const y=2;\\n  const z=3;\\n  return x+y+z;\\n}\\n' > a.js\nprintf 'function b(){\\n  const x=1;\\n  const y=2;\\n  const z=3;\\n  return x+y+z;\\n}\\n' > b.js\nprintf '{\"threshold\":0,\"minTokens\":10,\"minLines\":3,\"format\":\"console\",\"reporters\":[\"console\"]}' > .jscpd.json\n\nnpx --yes jscpd .\n```\n\nActual output:\n\n```\nFound 0 clones.\n```\n\nExit code `0` — the gate passes despite 100 % duplication between the two files.\n\nRemove `\"format\": \"console\"` (or set it to real languages) and re-run:\n\n```bash\nnpx --yes jscpd . --format javascript\n```\n\n```\nFound 1 clones.\nERROR: jscpd found too many duplicates (41.7%) over threshold (0.0%)\n```\n\nThis is not theoretical for real repositories either: in a repository using this template's config verbatim, `npx jscpd .` reports \"No duplicates found\", while `npx jscpd . --format \"javascript\"` on the same tree reports 24 files / 49 clones / **5.64 %** duplication.\n\n## Workaround\n\nOverride on the command line until the config is fixed:\n\n```bash\nnpx jscpd . --format \"javascript,typescript,jsx,tsx,markdown\"\n```\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nDrop the `format` key so jscpd uses its default language set, or list the languages the repository actually contains. `reporters` already carries the console output, so nothing is lost:\n\n```diff\n   \"ignore\": [\n     ...\n   ],\n-  \"format\": \"console\",\n   \"reporters\": [\"console\", \"html\"],\n   \"output\": \"./reports/jscpd\"\n }\n```\n\nor, to be explicit:\n\n```diff\n-  \"format\": \"console\",\n+  \"format\": [\"javascript\", \"jsx\", \"typescript\", \"tsx\", \"json\", \"markdown\", \"yaml\"],\n```\n\nNote that fixing this will make the gate start reporting real duplication, so repositories adopting the fix may need to set a non-zero `threshold` (or extend `ignore`) in the same change rather than being surprised by a suddenly red pipeline.\n\n## Suggested regression test\n\nSince the failure mode is silent, a check that jscpd actually analyzed something is worth adding to the workflow — e.g. assert the JSON reporter's `statistics.total.sources > 0`, so a future config typo fails loudly instead of turning the gate green.\n",
