+    "body": "Found while auditing a downstream repository against this template (link-assistant/agent#287). Two of the template's own rules are not applied to `release.yml` itself.\n\n## 1. `${{ github.head_ref }}` is interpolated into a shell script (injection)\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml` (changeset-check job):\n\n```yaml\n        env:\n          GITHUB_BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n          ...\n        run: |\n          if [[ \"${{ github.head_ref }}\" == \"changeset-release/\"* ]]; then\n```\n\n`github.head_ref` is the head branch name of a pull request, which for a fork PR is chosen by the contributor. Expressions are substituted into the script text *before* bash runs, so a branch named e.g. `a\"$(id>/tmp/x)\"b` executes as code in the `pull_request` job. The step already passes `github.base_ref` through `env:`; `head_ref` should be handled the same way:\n\n```yaml\n        env:\n          HEAD_REF: ${{ github.head_ref }}\n        run: |\n          if [[ \"$HEAD_REF\" == \"changeset-release/\"* ]]; then\n```\n\n## 2. `github.event.inputs.description` is interpolated into `run:` (injection)\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n        run: node scripts/version-and-commit.mjs --mode instant --bump-type \"${{ github.event.inputs.bump_type }}\" --description \"${{ github.event.inputs.description }}\"\n```\n\nand the same pattern in the changeset-pr job for `create-manual-changeset.mjs`. `description` is `type: string`, i.e. free-form, and these jobs hold the publishing permissions. `bump_type` is a `choice` so it is constrained, but `description` is not. Passing both through `env:` and reading them in the scripts keeps them as data.\n\n## 3. The default-branch env is missing from two of the three workflows\n\n`release.yml` sets\n\n```yaml\nenv:\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: init.defaultBranch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n```\n\nbut `example-app.yml` and `links.yml` do not, so every job in them logs `hint: Using 'master' as the name for the initial branch` from the `git init` that `actions/checkout` runs.\n\n## Suggested guard\n\nThese are all mechanically checkable, in the spirit of `tests/workflow-permissions.test.js`. The downstream repository added a rule that scans every `run:` block of every workflow for `/\\$\\{\\{\\s*(?:inputs\\.|github\\.event\\.inputs\\.|github\\.head_ref)[^}]*\\}\\}/` and a rule that requires `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: init.defaultBranch` in every workflow.\n",
