+    "body": "## Finding\n\nWhile fixing link-foundation/browser-commander#55, I compared the Browser Commander release workflow with this template and found two reusable CI/CD log-noise issues that can make successful releases look failed.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBrowser Commander run 28326104220 succeeded, but its release log printed:\n\n- `npm warn Unknown user config \"always-auth\"` after npm was upgraded for OIDC publishing\n- `npm error code E404` and `npm error 404 No match found for version 0.9.0` while checking that an unpublished version should be published\n\nThe current template still uses `npm view ... version` in `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs` for existence checks. That command is semantically useful, but npm prints expected misses as error lines. The template also does not sanitize the deprecated `always-auth` entry that setup-node can place in the npm user config for publishing.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- Check package version existence through the npm registry HTTP API instead of `npm view`, treating HTTP 404 as an expected false result without npm error output.\n- Remove `always-auth` from `$NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` after setup-node configures the npm registry and before npm commands run in publishing jobs.\n- Add unit tests for both helpers so this does not regress.\n\n## Related downstream fix\n\nBrowser Commander PR: https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/56",
