+    "body": "The numbers-vectorization issue https://github.com/konard/numbers-vectorization/issues/3 exposed a lychee false positive that appears to apply to this template too.\n\nThe template has a Vite source file at `examples/universal-app/index.html` with root-relative app asset URLs:\n\n- `/favicon.svg`\n- `/src/main.js`\n\nThe link workflow scans raw `*.html` files with lychee. In a repository checkout, lychee treats that source HTML as a local file rather than as Vite-served HTML, so root-relative app asset URLs can produce errors like:\n\n`Error building URL for \"/favicon.svg\": Cannot convert path '/favicon.svg' to a URI: To resolve root-relative links in local files, provide a root dir`\n\nIn numbers-vectorization, adding this args entry made the local lychee reproduction clean while keeping markdown checks enabled:\n\n`--exclude-path examples/universal-app/index.html`\n\nThe built/deployed app remains covered by the example-app workflow, while the link checker stays focused on repository documentation links.",
