+    "body": "## What\n\n- Adds a local ESLint rule, `local/no-changelog-comments`, configured at warning severity.\n- Scans comments, string literals, and template literal text for changelog-style source-history phrasing.\n- Covers English, Russian, Chinese, and Hindi markers, plus PR/issue/date references and allowlist options.\n- Adds focused tests for positive detections, false-positive guardrails, options, and Deno permission behavior.\n- Adds the requested issue case study and raw research snapshots under `docs/case-studies/issue-93`.\n- Hardens `scripts/detect-code-changes.mjs` to pass Git revisions as arguments, so Windows runners do not mangle `HEAD^` syntax through the shell.\n- Removes the initial placeholder `.gitkeep` commit file.\n\nFixes #93.\n\n## Notes\n\n`npm run lint` now surfaces an initial baseline of warning-level findings in existing scripts/tests for issue, PR, and date history references. This is intentional for the requested default-warn rollout; CI remains green unless the rule is later ratcheted to `error` or `--max-warnings 0`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/no-changelog-comments.test.js`\n- `node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/detect-code-changes.test.js`\n- `npm test`\n- `bun test --timeout 30000`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- `npm run check`\n- `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n",
