+    "body": "Fixes #86.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Parse `.changeset/*.md` files as changeset candidates only when their frontmatter declares the current package with a valid `major`, `minor`, or `patch` bump.\n- Reuse the repository's package path and package-name helpers so single-language and `js/` package layouts stay aligned with the other release scripts.\n- Add CLI regression coverage for stray Markdown docs, valid changesets, and valid-looking changesets for unknown packages.\n- Add the required patch changeset for the template behavior change.\n\n## Reproduction / Coverage\n\nBefore the fix, `.changeset/NOTES.md` with ordinary Markdown content made `scripts/check-changesets.mjs` report `has_changesets=true` and `changeset_count=1`. The new `tests/check-changesets.test.js` reproduces that fixture and asserts it now reports zero pending changesets, while still counting a real changeset for the detected package.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/check-changesets.test.js`\n- `bun test tests/check-changesets.test.js`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- `node scripts/check-changesets.mjs`\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `bash scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`\n- `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n",
