+    "body": "## Summary\n\n`merge-changesets` skips a malformed changeset with only a `console.warn`, so its bump and release notes silently vanish from the merged release instead of failing loudly.\n\n## Location\n\n`scripts/merge-changesets.mjs:131-133` and `148-149`\n\n```js\nconsole.warn(\n  `Warning: Could not parse version type from ${filePath}, skipping`\n);\n...\n} catch (error) {\n  console.warn(`Warning: Failed to parse ${filePath}: ${error.message}`);\n}\n```\n\n## Reproduction\n\nTwo changesets, one with broken frontmatter (e.g. a typo'd bump key). The valid one merges; the broken one is skipped with a warning. The release ships **without** the dropped changeset's bump/notes, and CI stays green — the loss is invisible unless someone reads the logs.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nTreat an unparseable changeset as a hard error (non-zero exit) so a malformed file blocks the release rather than being silently dropped — or at least surface it via `::error::` / a failing check, not `console.warn`.\n\n## Notes\n\nFound while auditing `link-assistant/web-search` (issue #17); the same behavior exists there.\n",
