+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `test` job in `.github/workflows/release.yml` runs the full test matrix on **changes that touch no code at all** (docs-only commits, `.gitkeep` edits, changeset-only commits). This wastes CI minutes and slows iteration.\n\n## Root cause\n\n```yaml\ntest:\n  needs: [detect-changes, changeset-check, test-compilation, lint, check-file-line-limits]\n  if: |\n    !cancelled() &&\n    (github.event_name == 'push' || needs.changeset-check.result == 'success' || needs.changeset-check.result == 'skipped') &&\n    (needs.test-compilation.result == 'success' || needs.test-compilation.result == 'skipped') &&\n    (needs.lint.result == 'success' || needs.lint.result == 'skipped') &&\n    (needs.check-file-line-limits.result == 'success' || needs.check-file-line-limits.result == 'skipped')\n```\n\nOn a non-code change, **every** upstream job is *skipped* (they all gate on `detect-changes`), so each clause matches its `== 'skipped'` branch and the whole condition is satisfied — `test` runs even though nothing relevant changed. The condition has **no positive \"did code change?\" gate**; it only checks that upstream jobs did not *fail*. `skipped` means \"no code changed at all,\" which is exactly when tests should NOT run.\n\n## Reproducible example\n\n1. Open a PR whose only change deletes a line from `.gitkeep` (or edits a `*.md` file).\n2. `test-compilation`, `lint`, `check-file-line-limits`, `changeset-check` all **skip**, yet **`test` still runs**.\n\nConfirmed downstream in `link-assistant/formal-ai#442` (a sibling pipeline) where the analogous defect ran the full suite for a one-line `.gitkeep` deletion.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdd an explicit change-detector gate (keep the existing fast-check `== 'skipped'` guards — those are legitimate). The **python template** is the correct reference: gate on the `detect-changes` outputs.\n\n```yaml\ntest:\n  if: |\n    !cancelled() &&\n    (\n      github.event_name == 'push' ||\n      needs.detect-changes.outputs.any-code-changed == 'true' ||\n      needs.detect-changes.outputs.mjs-changed == 'true' ||\n      needs.detect-changes.outputs.js-changed == 'true' ||\n      needs.detect-changes.outputs.package-changed == 'true' ||\n      needs.detect-changes.outputs.workflow-changed == 'true'\n    ) &&\n    (github.event_name == 'push' || needs.changeset-check.result == 'success' || needs.changeset-check.result == 'skipped') &&\n    (needs.test-compilation.result == 'success' || needs.test-compilation.result == 'skipped') &&\n    (needs.lint.result == 'success' || needs.lint.result == 'skipped') &&\n    (needs.check-file-line-limits.result == 'success' || needs.check-file-line-limits.result == 'skipped')\n```\n\n## General principle\n\nGate jobs on **change-detector outputs**, never *solely* on whether sibling jobs were skipped. `skipped` is ambiguous (it can mean \"irrelevant change\" or \"nothing changed\") and inverts easily. rust/csharp/js templates share this defect; the python template is the correct reference.\n\n_Reported from the downstream fix in link-assistant/formal-ai#442 / link-assistant/formal-ai#443._\n",
