+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `publish-dockerhub` composite action boots buildx with `docker/setup-buildx-action@v4` (then `docker/build-push-action@v7`) and no pinned-image pre-pull. The default `docker-container` driver makes dockerd pull `moby/buildkit:buildx-stable-1` from Docker Hub at boot. When `registry-1.docker.io` has a transient outage, that boot pull fails and takes the whole publish job down — even though nothing is wrong with the code or the build.\n\nThis is the same class of failure investigated downstream in `link-foundation/box` issue #100 (a ~2.5-minute Docker Hub registry outage failed the buildx boot) and originally issue #97.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nAny release run where `registry-1.docker.io` is unreachable for longer than a normal blip will fail at **Set up Docker Buildx → Creating a new builder instance** with:\n\n```\nERROR: Error response from daemon: Get \"https://registry-1.docker.io/v2/\": net/http: request canceled while waiting for connection (Client.Timeout exceeded while awaiting headers)\n```\n\nYou can simulate it by blocking `registry-1.docker.io` (e.g. a hosts/iptables blackhole) on a runner and then running the buildx step.\n\n## Workaround\n\nRe-run the job once Docker Hub recovers.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nPre-pull the pinned BuildKit image before booting, with a retry loop **and a pull-through registry-mirror fallback** (`mirror.gcr.io`, on independent infrastructure), then re-tag it to the canonical reference so the boot reuses the local copy and never touches the failing registry. `link-foundation/box` implements this as a reusable composite action `setup-buildx-resilient`:\n\n- Action: `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient/action.yml`\n- Case study: `docs/case-studies/issue-100/CASE-STUDY.md`\n\nMinimal sketch:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Pre-pull BuildKit image (retry + mirror fallback)\n  shell: bash\n  run: |\n    img=moby/buildkit:buildx-stable-1\n    pull() { for d in 5 10 20 40 0; do docker pull \"$1\" && return 0; sleep \"$d\"; done; return 1; }\n    pull \"$img\" && exit 0\n    pull \"mirror.gcr.io/$img\" && { docker tag \"mirror.gcr.io/$img\" \"$img\"; exit 0; }\n    echo \"::warning::could not pre-pull $img; letting buildx try its own boot pull\"\n- name: Set up Docker Buildx\n  uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v4\n  with:\n    driver-opts: image=moby/buildkit:buildx-stable-1\n```\n\nHappy to port the full resilient action over if useful.\n",
