+    "body": "## Summary\n\n`.github/workflows/links.yml` (Broken Link Checker) does **not** declare a `concurrency:` block, while its sibling workflows in the same template do:\n\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml` →\n  ```yaml\n  concurrency:\n    group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n    cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}\n  ```\n- `.github/workflows/example-app.yml` → same block.\n\nBecause `links.yml` is triggered on `push` (main) and `pull_request` (`opened`/`synchronize`/`reopened`) just like the others, pushing several commits in quick succession to the same branch/PR leaves **redundant link-check runs in flight** instead of cancelling the superseded ones. That wastes CI minutes and slows feedback — the exact problem the `concurrency` block solves elsewhere in this template.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdd the same block the sibling workflows already use, immediately after the `on:` section:\n\n```yaml\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}\n```\n\nThe `github.ref != 'refs/heads/main'` guard keeps the main-branch run from being cancelled mid-flight while still cancelling redundant PR/branch runs — consistent with the rest of the template.\n\n## Cross-reference\n\nFound while comparing CI/CD across the `js`/`rust`/`python`/`csharp` ai-driven-development-pipeline-templates for downstream repo [`link-foundation/box`](https://github.com/link-foundation/box) (issue #94 / PR #95). The other three templates have `concurrency` on every workflow; `links.yml` here is the only workflow across all four templates that is missing it.",
