+    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe template `scripts/create-github-release.mjs` sends the extracted changelog entry as the GitHub Release API `body` without a size guard. A downstream Rust repository accumulated a very large changelog section and GitHub release creation started failing with HTTP 422 validation errors after the package registry publish had already succeeded.\n\nDownstream issue and evidence: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/390\n\n## Reproducible example\n\n1. Add a very large section for the next version in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n2. Run `node scripts/create-github-release.mjs --release-version 1.2.3 --repository OWNER/REPO`.\n3. GitHub release creation can fail at the API validation step because the generated release body is too large.\n\n## Workaround\n\nShorten the release body manually before creating the GitHub release, or create the release manually with a summary and a link to the full changelog.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nCap the generated GitHub release body to a conservative byte limit before calling `gh api`, preserve the beginning of the changelog entry, and append a note linking to the full tagged `CHANGELOG.md`. Add a regression test that feeds an oversized changelog entry and asserts the generated payload stays under the guard limit.\n",
