+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `preview-regen` job in `.github/workflows/example-app.yml` installs the\nPlaywright Chromium browser with no per-step timeout, no retry, and no browser\ncache. The Playwright CDN (`cdn.playwright.dev`) can stall a download after the\nbytes finish transferring, with **no internal timeout**, hanging the step until\nthe job-level `timeout-minutes` fires. This wastes a full runner-timeout window\n(~20 min) on every transient stall and re-downloads the ~170 MiB browser on\nevery run.\n\n## Where\n\n`.github/workflows/example-app.yml`, job `preview-regen`:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Install browser automation dependencies\n  env:\n    PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_BROWSER_DOWNLOAD: '1'   # good: postinstall download skipped\n  run: npm install --no-save --package-lock=false --no-audit --no-fund browser-commander@0.8.1 playwright@1.59.1\n\n- name: Install Chromium for preview rendering\n  run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium   # <-- no timeout, no retry, no cache\n```\n\nThe `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_BROWSER_DOWNLOAD: '1'` guard on the npm install is correct,\nbut the subsequent explicit `npx playwright install` is unguarded.\n\n## Impact observed downstream\n\nWe hit this exact stall in `link-assistant/hive-mind` (a near-identical\npreview-regen + e2e Pages workflow modelled on this template): the Chromium\ndownload reached 100% of 170.4 MiB, then the connection stalled on the next\nasset with no timeout and the job hung for ~22 minutes before the runner\ncancelled it.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nTwo complementary mitigations (both already validated downstream):\n\n1. **Cache the browser** so most runs skip the download entirely:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Cache Playwright browsers\n  uses: actions/cache@v4\n  with:\n    path: ~/.cache/ms-playwright\n    key: playwright-1.59.1-${{ runner.os }}\n```\n\n2. **Wrap the install in a `timeout` + retry loop** so a transient stall\n   self-heals instead of consuming the whole job window:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Install Chromium for preview rendering (retry on stalled download)\n  run: |\n    for attempt in 1 2 3; do\n      if timeout 360 npx playwright install --with-deps chromium; then\n        echo \"Playwright Chromium installed on attempt $attempt\"\n        exit 0\n      fi\n      echo \"::warning::Playwright install attempt $attempt failed or timed out; retrying in 10s\"\n      sleep 10\n    done\n    echo \"::error::Playwright Chromium install failed after 3 attempts\"\n    exit 1\n```\n\nPinning the cache key to the Playwright version (`playwright-1.59.1-...`) keeps\nthe cache correct across upgrades.\n\n## Context\n\nReported while comparing CI/CD workflows in `link-assistant/hive-mind` against\nthis template (link-assistant/hive-mind#1838). Happy to open a PR with the fix\nif useful.\n",
