+    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe template's line-limit CI does not fully enforce the documented architecture limit across JavaScript and Markdown files.\n\nCurrent gaps observed from the template:\n- scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh only checks .mjs files and .github/workflows/release.yml.\n- ESLint covers JavaScript source files, but the shell gate misses .js and .cjs files when ESLint is not the relevant path.\n- Documentation validation uses a 2500-line Markdown limit instead of the 1500-line architecture limit.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe CI line-limit gate should enforce the documented maximum for tracked JavaScript and Markdown files, with any intentional case-study or generated-data exception called out explicitly.\n\n## Source\n\nFound while addressing link-assistant/meta-expression#54 / PR link-assistant/meta-expression#55, which needed the same correction for Rust, JavaScript, and Markdown files.",
