+    "body": "Downstream context from `link-assistant/meta-expression` PR 51 / issue 50: the generated JS workflow matrix runs 9 test jobs (`node`, `bun`, `deno` across `ubuntu-latest`, `macos-latest`, and `windows-latest`). In that downstream PR, the latest `JS Checks and release` run failed in `Test (node on windows-latest)` before tests started, during `actions/checkout@v6`:\n\n```text\nfatal: Cannot prompt because user interactivity has been disabled.\nfatal: could not read Username for 'https://github.com': terminal prompts disabled\nThe process 'C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\git.exe' failed with exit code 128\n```\n\nThe project maintainer requested using only Bun on Linux for JavaScript tests to reduce unstable runner/runtime combinations and speed up iterations. Node is still needed for lint/release scripts, but Node/Deno/macOS/Windows test jobs should be opt-in rather than the default for projects that standardize on Bun/Linux.\n\nTemplate locations observed in the current tree:\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: test matrix comment says `3 runtimes (Node.js, Bun, Deno) x 3 OS`.\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: matrix uses `os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest]` and `runtime: [node, bun, deno]`.\n\nSuggested fix:\n- Provide a Bun/Linux-only JS test mode or make it the default template behavior.\n- Keep fast checks, lint, changeset/version checks, and release jobs on Ubuntu.\n- Keep Node setup where scripts require Node, but remove Node/Deno/macOS/Windows from the test matrix unless explicitly enabled.\n\nWorkaround for generated repositories:\n- In the JS test job, use only `runs-on: ubuntu-latest` with `oven-sh/setup-bun` and `bun test`.\n",
