+    "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo independent CI/CD issues in this template.\n\n### 1. Reversed `cancel-in-progress` condition\n\nBoth `example-app.yml:32` and `release.yml:42` use:\n\n```yaml\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}\n```\n\nThe `==` should be `!=`. With the current condition:\n\n- **On `main`** the value evaluates to `true`, so a follow-up push to `main` (e.g. an automated currency/data update or a manual fix landing while a release is in flight) **cancels** the still-running release pipeline.\n- **On a PR branch** the value evaluates to `false`, so every PR push starts a new run that races the previous one. Slow PR runs waste CI minutes.\n\nThe intent is the opposite: protect main from concurrent cancellation, and let PR pushes supersede older runs.\n\n**Recommended fix:**\n\n```yaml\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}\n```\n\n### 2. `preview-regen` job has no failure-artifact upload\n\n`example-app.yml`'s `preview-regen` job (lines ~197-268) runs Playwright/Chromium to render preview screenshots, but has no `if: failure()` step that uploads the test-results, playwright traces, or partial screenshots. When the job fails (e.g. when a selector is wrong or the preview server hangs), the run page contains no artifacts a human can use to debug — only the raw step log.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Add a step before/after the screenshot step:\n\n\\`\\`\\`yaml\n- name: Upload screenshot failure artifacts\n  if: failure()\n  uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\n  with:\n    name: preview-regen-failure-\\${{ github.run_id }}\n    path: |\n      docs/screenshots/\n      web/test-results/\n      web/playwright-report/\n    retention-days: 7\n    if-no-files-found: ignore\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Where this was discovered\n\nFound while applying template best practices to \\`link-assistant/calculator\\` PR #157 (https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/pull/157). The screenshot job there hit exactly the gap described in (2) — failures were unreproducible from the run page. Both issues reported across sibling templates for consistency.",
