+    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #62.\n\nAdds a release-time `preview-regen` job to `.github/workflows/example-app.yml` plus `scripts/update-preview-images.mjs` that boot the universal example app in a headless Chromium via `browser-commander` + Playwright, capture a locale × theme matrix of screenshots into `docs/screenshots/example-app/`, and commit drift back to `main` with `[skip ci]`.\n\nPattern reused from [konard/vk-bot-desktop#52](https://github.com/konard/vk-bot-desktop/pull/52) (closes konard/vk-bot-desktop#51), adapted to this template's structure (Vite-built `examples/universal-app`, `@link-foundation/example-package-name` changeset).\n\n## What's included\n\n- **`scripts/update-preview-images.mjs`** — boots `examples/universal-app/dist` via a Node http static server, walks a 2×2 locale × theme matrix (`en`/`ru` × `light`/`dark`), drives Chromium through `browser-commander` (with verbose mode behind `PREVIEW_VERBOSE=1`), waits for `.app-shell` + `#calculator-title`, and writes `docs/screenshots/example-app/example-app-{locale}-{theme}.png`. Copies the `en-light` tile to `example-app.png` as the README fallback. `--skip-build` reuses any existing `dist`.\n- **`preview-regen` job in `example-app.yml`** — runs on push-to-main and `workflow_dispatch`, installs `browser-commander@0.8.1` + `playwright@1.59.1` with `--no-save --package-lock=false` (so the root lockfile is not mutated), installs Chromium with `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`, regenerates screenshots, and commits any drift back to `main` with `[skip ci]` to avoid re-triggering itself.\n- **`example:web:preview-images` npm script** — `node scripts/update-preview-images.mjs` for local repro.\n- **Docs** — root `README.md` gains an \"Auto-regenerated preview screenshots\" section under \"Deploying the example app\" and a Scripts Reference row; `examples/universal-app/README.md` embeds the generated preview image with a note pointing at the workflow.\n- **Test coverage** — new test in `tests/universal-app.test.js` asserts the npm script, workflow snippets (`preview-regen:`, `browser-commander`, `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`, `[skip ci]`), script imports (`from 'browser-commander'`, `from 'playwright'`), output path, and README snippets are all present.\n- **Changeset** — `.changeset/preview-regen-pipeline.md` (`'@link-foundation/example-package-name': minor`).\n\n## Why a 2×2 matrix when the example app has no i18n/themes yet\n\nThe script is template-ready: downstream forks that add a `data-theme` attribute or `lang` switching get matrix coverage without touching the script. `browser.newContext({ locale, colorScheme })` + `commander.emulateMedia({ colorScheme })` plus a seeded `localStorage.theme` cover the common patterns. Today all four tiles render identically (114 520 bytes each), which is the documented baseline.\n\n## Preview image\n\n![Universal example app preview](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/blob/issue-62-768f27a1146b/docs/screenshots/example-app/example-app.png?raw=true)\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` — all 62 tests pass, including the new `regenerates preview screenshots with browser-commander on every push to main` case.\n- [x] `npm run check` — ESLint (max-lines 1500, max-lines-per-function 150), Prettier, and jscpd all clean.\n- [x] `node scripts/update-preview-images.mjs` — locally regenerates all 5 PNGs (4 matrix tiles + fallback) under `docs/screenshots/example-app/`.\n- [x] `node scripts/update-preview-images.mjs --skip-build` — reuses existing `dist/`.\n- [x] `PREVIEW_VERBOSE=1 node scripts/update-preview-images.mjs --skip-build` — verbose mode prints PNG signatures and the resolved `<html data-theme>` / `<html lang>` probe.\n- [ ] CI verifies the new test case on this PR.\n- [ ] After merge, the first push to `main` triggers `preview-regen` and either confirms no drift or auto-commits the refreshed screenshots with `[skip ci]`.\n",
