+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe current `example-app.yml` deploys to GitHub Pages on every push to `main` using `actions/configure-pages@v6` + `actions/upload-pages-artifact@v5` + `actions/deploy-pages@v5`. The pattern is correct, but the first time a downstream repository runs it, the deploy job fails with `Error: Get Pages site failed.` / `Error: Failed to create deployment` if **Settings → Pages → Source** is not set to **GitHub Actions** (it defaults to *Deploy from a branch*).\n\nThis bit several downstream consumers, including [link-foundation/relative-meta-logic#163](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/issues/163) (fixed in [PR #170](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/pull/170)). The workflow rewrite alone is necessary but not sufficient; the maintainer also has to flip the Pages source. This cannot be automated from inside a workflow.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdd a `## Deploying the example app` section to `README.md` of this template that says, in essentially these words:\n\n> Before the first run on `main`, open **Settings → Pages** of the new repository and set **Source = GitHub Actions**. This is a one-time manual step and cannot be configured from a workflow. The workflow will then provision the Pages site on its first run.\n\nOptionally, add a comment to that effect right above the `pages-deploy` job in `example-app.yml`.\n\n## Reproducible example\n\n1. Bootstrap a new repository from this template.\n2. Push to `main` without touching repository settings.\n3. Observe that `pages-deploy` fails on `actions/deploy-pages@v5` with `Get Pages site failed`.\n4. Set **Settings → Pages → Source = GitHub Actions**, re-run; the deploy succeeds.",
