+    "body": "While working on link-assistant/router#23 and comparing against link-assistant/hive-mind, I found that this JS CI/CD template does not currently provide an optional Docker Hub publish path for projects that ship Docker images. Hive Mind keeps Docker publishing downstream of the npm release and uses the exact published package version for Docker tags.\\n\\nRecommended follow-up:\\n- Add an optional Docker Hub image publish pattern using Docker's official GitHub Actions.\\n- Use DOCKERHUB_TOKEN for registry authentication.\\n- Ensure Docker publish waits for the matching npm package version before tagging images.\\n- Add static checks that verify package-before-Docker release ordering and version-tag parity.\\n\\nReference implementation in progress for the Rust router: https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/24",
