+    "body": "## Problem\\n\\nWhile investigating link-foundation/start#122, I found the same release-helper failure mode in this template's scripts/create-github-release.mjs. The script runs:\\n\\n```js\\nawait $`gh api repos/${repository}/releases -X POST --input -`.run({ stdin: payload });\\nconsole.log(`✅ Created GitHub release: ${tag}`);\\n```\\n\\nIn the downstream start repository, command-stream returned a non-zero result from `gh api` for GitHub HTTP 422 / `already_exists`, but the script did not inspect the result code and printed a successful release message anyway. That produced a green release job even though the intended GitHub release was not created.\\n\\n## Reproduction pattern\\n\\n1. Ensure a release/tag already exists.\\n2. Run `scripts/create-github-release.mjs` for that same tag.\\n3. `gh api` returns a validation failure such as `already_exists`.\\n4. The current script can still print `Created GitHub release` because it does not validate the command result.\\n\\n## Suggested fix\\n\\nUse native child process execution or explicitly inspect the command-stream result code. Treat unexpected non-zero exits as failures, and treat `already_exists` as an idempotent skip only if that behavior is desired and clearly logged as a skip. Add a regression test with a fake `gh` executable that exits non-zero.",
