+    "body": "## Problem\n\nNeither `.github/workflows/release.yml` nor `.github/workflows/links.yml` declares `timeout-minutes` on any job. Without an explicit cap, GitHub Actions falls back to its default of **six hours per job**. A flaky network call or a hung promise then blocks the AI iteration loop for hours instead of failing in minutes.\n\nThe same gap exists at the test-runner level: `npm test` runs `node --test tests/*.test.js` without `--test-timeout`, so an individual test can also hang for the full job duration before the job-level cap (if any) trips.\n\nThis defeats the \"fail fast to fix flaky tests faster\" property that AI-driven development depends on — the AI can only iterate as fast as CI gives it feedback.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\n# In the template's own .github/workflows/:\n$ grep -rn timeout-minutes .github/workflows/\n# (no matches)\n\n$ grep -rn -- '--test-timeout\\|--timeout' .github/workflows/\n# (no matches)\n```\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nAdopt the bands we landed in `link-foundation/meta-sovereign` after observing actual job p95s. Sized at roughly 5–10× the observed p95 so a real run never trips the cap, but a hung run fails in minutes:\n\n| Band | Jobs |\n|------|------|\n| 5 min | `detect-changes`, `test-compilation`, `check-file-line-limits`, `version-check`, `validate-docs` |\n| 10 min | `changeset-check`, `lint`, `test` (per runtime × OS), `links-checker`, `changeset-pr` |\n| 15 min | `docs-build` |\n| 30 min | `release`, `instant-release` |\n\nPer-test budget (so a hung individual test fails in 30s, not at the job cap):\n\n```json\n\"scripts\": {\n  \"test\": \"node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/*.test.js\"\n}\n```\n\n```yaml\n# CI bun runner step\n- run: bun test --timeout 30000\n```\n\nDeno has no global per-test timeout flag, so Deno tests stay protected only by the job-level `timeout-minutes: 10`.\n\n## Reference implementation\n\nLanded in https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/pull/2 (commit 5c5fdcc). Includes:\n\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml` + `links.yml` with `timeout-minutes` on every job, each with an inline comment recording the typical run vs. the cap so future tuning is data-driven\n- `package.json` `test` script with `--test-timeout=30000`\n- `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md` §13 \"Reasonable Timeouts on Every Job and Test\" codifying the policy\n- `README.md` testing section summarising the policy for contributors\n\nHappy to open a PR mirroring those changes against this template if useful.",
