+    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #40.\n\nThis PR fixes the release-note npm badge formatter for prefixed release tags such as `js-v1.7.12` and `rust-v0.3.4`. The formatter now extracts the semantic version before building the npm badge, escapes shields.io static badge message separators, and keeps links pointed at the exact npm package version.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `scripts/format-release-notes-helpers.mjs` for release-version normalization and shields.io static badge path escaping.\n- Updated `scripts/format-release-notes.mjs` to use the helper instead of `version.replace(/^v/, '')`.\n- Added regression tests for plain `v`, `js-v`, `rust-v`, and prefixed prerelease tags.\n- Added a patch changeset.\n- Added `docs/case-studies/issue-40/` with issue/PR data, CI logs, live shields.io SVG evidence, downstream web-capture evidence, Rust-template snapshots, and CI/CD comparison notes.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nBefore the fix, this shields.io URL returns a `404: badge not found` SVG:\n\n```sh\ncurl -sS 'https://img.shields.io/badge/npm-js-v1.7.12-blue.svg' | head -c 200\n```\n\nThe normalized form returns `npm: 1.7.12`:\n\n```sh\ncurl -sS 'https://img.shields.io/badge/npm-1.7.12-blue.svg' | head -c 200\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test tests/release-badge.test.js`\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `bash scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`\n- `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n- `node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `npx --yes -p secretlint -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend secretlint \"**/*\"`\n\n## Rust Template Check\n\nThe Rust template was checked at `353d89396fd420339f2dab0e548ca2caf6198cd5`. It uses dynamic `img.shields.io/crates/v/<crate>` badges instead of static `/badge/<label>-<message>-<color>` npm badges, so this exact issue was not present there and no Rust-template issue was filed.\n",
