+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe current `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` enforces a hard 1500-line limit but has **no warn band**. Two PRs that each individually keep a file under 1500 can together push it over after both merge — the second PR's CI passes pre-merge, then the post-merge check on `main` is the first failure signal. Downstream Docker / Helm / Release jobs are then gated and skipped until someone notices.\n\nThis pattern has bitten downstream consumers of the template repeatedly:\n\n- [`link-assistant/hive-mind` issue #1593](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1593) — original concurrent-merge race.\n- [`link-assistant/hive-mind` issue #1730](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1730) — same shape, single PR adding a small block to many files near the threshold; case study at <https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/case-studies/issue-1730/README.md>.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. In any repo using this template, prepare two PRs that each modify the same `.mjs` file.\n2. Each PR alone leaves the file under 1500 lines (e.g. file is at 1499, PR-A adds 1 line, PR-B adds 1 line).\n3. Merge PR-A. Merge PR-B. Both CI runs were green pre-merge.\n4. The first CI run on `main` after PR-B fails: `ERROR: file has 1500 lines (limit: 1500)` (or above).\n5. Release / build jobs are skipped because `check-file-line-limits` is a required gate.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nPort the `WARN_THRESHOLD=1350` band from `link-assistant/hive-mind`'s version of the script. The 150-line gap (10% headroom) is enough to absorb typical concurrent-PR drift without being so tight that benign refactors are noisy.\n\nPatch (functionally what hive-mind does today):\n\n```bash\nLIMIT=1500\nWARN_THRESHOLD=1350\nFAILURES=()\nWARNINGS=()\n\n# inside the find loop, after the >LIMIT check:\nelif [ \"\\$line_count\" -gt \"\\$WARN_THRESHOLD\" ]; then\n  WARNINGS+=(\\\"\\$file\\\")\nfi\n\n# after the loop, before the failure summary:\nif [ \\\"\\${#WARNINGS[@]}\\\" -gt 0 ]; then\n  echo \\\"\\\"\n  echo \\\"The following files are approaching the \\${LIMIT} line limit (>\\${WARN_THRESHOLD} lines):\\\"\n  printf '  %s\\n' \\\"\\${WARNINGS[@]}\\\"\n  echo \\\"\\\"\n  echo \\\"Consider extracting code to prevent concurrent PR merge limit violations.\\\"\nfi\n```\n\nHive-mind's version is here for reference: <https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh>.\n\nOptionally, project owners can promote warnings to errors in PRs that touch warn-band files, but the warn-only behavior is sufficient on its own — it gives reviewers a visible cue to pause and refactor before the file becomes a concurrent-merge hazard.\n\n## Out-of-scope follow-up\n\nWhile auditing the template against the same downstream incident, I noticed:\n\n- The template's `eslint.config.js` already uses the shorthand `'max-lines': ['error', 1500]` (defaults `skipBlankLines: false, skipComments: false`), so it does **not** have the ESLint-vs-CI desync bug we just fixed in hive-mind. No change needed there.\n\nJust adding the warn band would close the remaining gap.",
