+    "body": "## Summary\n\n`scripts/format-release-notes.mjs` only strips a single leading `v` before interpolating the release version into a shields.io `/badge/<label>-<message>-<color>` URL. When the caller passes a language-prefixed tag such as `js-v1.7.12` or `rust-v0.3.4`, the resulting URL contains extra unescaped `-` separators and shields.io returns the SVG `404: badge not found`.\n\nThis template works correctly for consumers that use a plain `v<version>` tag, but any downstream repo that multiplexes JS and Rust releases under `js-v<version>` / `rust-v<version>` tags hits the bug. For concrete evidence see [link-assistant/web-capture#98](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/issues/98) and the [fix PR link-assistant/web-capture#99](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/pull/99).\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS 'https://img.shields.io/badge/npm-js-v1.7.12-blue.svg' | head -c 200\n```\n\nReturns an SVG whose `aria-label=\"404: badge not found\"`. The working form is:\n\n```bash\ncurl -sS 'https://img.shields.io/badge/npm-1.7.12-blue.svg' | head -c 200\n```\n\nWhich returns `aria-label=\"npm: 1.7.12\"`.\n\n## Offending line\n\n`scripts/format-release-notes.mjs`:\n\n```js\nconst versionWithoutV = version.replace(/^v/, '');\n```\n\n`version.replace(/^v/, '')` strips a leading single `v`. Given `js-v1.7.12`, `versionWithoutV` stays `js-v1.7.12`, and the next line interpolates it into a URL with four `-`-separated fields instead of the three that shields.io parses.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nPick one of the following. All are backward-compatible with consumers that pass a plain `v<version>`:\n\n1. **Normalize the passed string** (what link-assistant/web-capture#99 ships):\n\n   ```js\n   const versionWithoutV = version\n     .replace(/^[a-z]+-/i, '')   // drop \"js-\", \"rust-\", etc.\n     .replace(/^v/i, '');        // drop leading \"v\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Use the dynamic shields endpoint** so the badge reads the current npm version directly and does not depend on the tag string:\n\n   ```js\n   const npmBadge = `[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/${PACKAGE_NAME}?label=npm&color=blue)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/${PACKAGE_NAME})`;\n   ```\n\n3. **Encourage callers to pass the clean numeric version** from `steps.publish.outputs.published_version` rather than the tag. `scripts/format-github-release.mjs` currently passes the full tag - it could strip the prefix at the call site instead.\n\n## Workaround for affected downstreams\n\nUntil upstream fixes this, downstream consumers can override the version normalization as in link-assistant/web-capture@7ee8fe6 and optionally run a one-shot repair like [link-assistant/web-capture's fix-existing-release-badges.mjs](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/blob/main/scripts/fix-existing-release-badges.mjs) against already-published releases.\n\n## Related\n\n- Rust pipeline template sidesteps the issue because it uses `/crates/v/<name>` (dynamic) rather than `/badge/...` (static).\n- shields.io /badge syntax reference: https://shields.io/badges/static-badge",
