+    "body": "## Problem\n\n`scripts/create-github-release.mjs` hardcodes `v${version}` as the GitHub release tag:\n\n```js\n// Line 53 of scripts/create-github-release.mjs\nconst tag = `v${version}`;\n```\n\nSimilarly, `scripts/format-github-release.mjs` hardcodes the same pattern:\n\n```js\n// Line 57 of scripts/format-github-release.mjs\nconst tag = `v${version}`;\n```\n\nWhen this template is used in a **multi-language repository** (e.g., one repo with both a JS and a Rust package), tag names collide or are ambiguous:\n\n- `v1.7.8` — is this a JS release or a Rust release?\n\nThe Rust equivalent in the Rust template uses `rust-v<version>` to be explicit.\n\n## Workaround\n\nIn downstream repos, manually change the tag to `js-v${version}` in both scripts. This is what was done in [link-assistant/web-capture#89](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/pull/89) to fix [issue #88](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/issues/88).\n\n## Suggested Fix\n\nChange `scripts/create-github-release.mjs`:\n\n```js\n// Before:\nconst tag = `v${version}`;\nname: version,\n\n// After:\nconst tag = `js-v${version}`;\nname: `JS v${version}`,\n```\n\nChange `scripts/format-github-release.mjs`:\n\n```js\n// Before:\nconst tag = `v${version}`;\n\n// After:\nconst tag = `js-v${version}`;\n```\n\nOr better, add a `--tag-prefix` CLI parameter (defaulting to `v`) so template users can override it without modifying the script:\n\n```js\n.option('tag-prefix', {\n  type: 'string',\n  default: getenv('TAG_PREFIX', 'v'),\n  describe: 'Prefix for the git tag (e.g., \"js-v\" for multi-language repos)',\n})\n// ...\nconst tag = `${tagPrefix}${version}`;\n```\n\nAnd pass it from the workflow:\n\n```yaml\nrun: node scripts/create-github-release.mjs --release-version \"...\" --repository \"...\" --tag-prefix \"js-\"\n```\n\n## Reproducible Example\n\n1. Clone this template.\n2. Set up a repo that also has a Rust package using the Rust template.\n3. Trigger a JS release — tag will be `v1.0.0`.\n4. Trigger a Rust release — tag will be `rust-v1.0.0`.\n5. The JS release tag `v1.0.0` is ambiguous; should be `js-v1.0.0`.",
