+    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #36\n\n- Add `scripts/check-release-needed.mjs` — checks npm registry to detect unpublished versions, enabling releases even without changesets (analogous to Rust template's `check-release-needed.rs`)\n- Update `release.yml` — integrate the new script as a self-healing fallback path in the release job\n- Add case study documentation in `docs/case-studies/issue-36/`\n\n## Problem\n\nThe release job was gated entirely on the presence of changeset files. If a PR merged without a changeset, the release job silently did nothing, leaving merged fixes unreleased indefinitely. This was documented in [link-assistant/web-capture#56](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/issues/56).\n\n## Solution\n\nThe new `check-release-needed.mjs` script runs after `check-changesets` and checks the npm registry:\n\n1. **Changesets exist** → normal flow (`should_release=true`, `skip_bump=false`)\n2. **No changesets, version not on npm** → self-healing (`should_release=true`, `skip_bump=true`) — publishes the current version directly\n3. **No changesets, version already on npm** → no action needed (`should_release=false`)\n\nThe publish step in `release.yml` now has a third condition for the self-healing path:\n\n```yaml\nif: >-\n  steps.version.outputs.version_committed == 'true' ||\n  steps.version.outputs.already_released == 'true' ||\n  (steps.check_release.outputs.should_release == 'true' && steps.check_release.outputs.skip_bump == 'true')\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Verified `check-release-needed.mjs` outputs correct values with `HAS_CHANGESETS=true`\n- [x] Verified self-healing path with `HAS_CHANGESETS=false` (detects `my-package@0.7.1` not on npm)\n- [x] Verified default behavior when `HAS_CHANGESETS` env var is unset\n- [x] All local CI checks pass (eslint, prettier, tests, syntax check, file line limits)\n- [x] Experiment test script at `experiments/test-check-release-needed.mjs`\n- [ ] CI checks on PR\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
