+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `release` job in `release.yml` gates publishing entirely on the presence of changeset files in `.changeset/`. If a PR merges to main without a changeset (which can happen for bugfixes, CI changes, dependency bumps, etc.), the release job silently does nothing, leaving merged fixes unreleased indefinitely.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `release.yml` lines 390-407:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Check for changesets\n  id: check_changesets\n  run: node scripts/check-changesets.mjs\n\n- name: Version packages and commit to main\n  if: steps.check_changesets.outputs.has_changesets == 'true'\n  ...\n\n- name: Publish to npm\n  if: steps.version.outputs.version_committed == 'true' || steps.version.outputs.already_released == 'true'\n```\n\nThe entire release flow is gated on `has_changesets == 'true'`. No changesets → no version step → no publish → no release.\n\n## Impact\n\nUsers running `npm install <package>` get a stale version that doesn't include merged fixes. This is the exact issue documented in link-assistant/web-capture#56.\n\n## Comparison with Rust Template\n\nThe [rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template) already handles this correctly via `check-release-needed.rs`, which:\n1. Checks crates.io (not just local state) to determine if the current version is published\n2. If the version isn't published, proceeds with release even without fragments\n3. Acts as a self-healing mechanism for accumulated unreleased changes\n\n## Suggested Fix\n\nAdd a `check-release-needed.mjs` script (analogous to the Rust template's `check-release-needed.rs`) that:\n\n1. Checks npm registry to see if the current `package.json` version is published\n2. If not published → signal release needed (no changeset required)\n3. If published → check for unreleased commits since the last release tag that touch publishable paths\n4. If unreleased publishable changes found → auto-bump patch version and release\n\nThis ensures the pipeline is **self-healing**: any push to main that includes unreleased code will trigger a release, regardless of whether a changeset was included.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Create a PR that changes `src/` files without adding a `.changeset/*.md` file\n2. Merge the PR to main\n3. Observe that the release job in CI runs but publishes nothing\n4. `npm view <package> version` still shows the old version\n\n## Related\n\n- link-assistant/web-capture#56 — same issue in a downstream project using this template\n- link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template — already has the fix via `check-release-needed.rs`",
