+    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe `scripts/detect-code-changes.mjs` script compares `GITHUB_BASE_SHA...GITHUB_HEAD_SHA` for pull request events, which returns **all files changed across the entire PR**, not just what the latest push changed.\n\nThis means a commit that only modifies non-code files (e.g. `.gitkeep`, `README.md`) will still trigger all CI jobs if any earlier commit in the same PR touched code files.\n\n### Evidence\n\nIn [link-assistant/web-capture PR #49](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/pull/49), commit `0e9b6e8c` only modified `.gitkeep` but triggered all 8 CI jobs (lint, test on 3 OSes, build, changeset check) because the PR as a whole contained code changes.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nGitHub Actions checks out a **synthetic merge commit** for \\`pull_request\\` events:\n- \\`HEAD\\` = merge commit\n- \\`HEAD^\\` = base branch (first parent)\n- \\`HEAD^2\\` = actual PR head commit (second parent)\n\nUsing \\`git diff HEAD^ HEAD\\` gives the full PR diff (base branch → merge), not the per-commit diff.\n\n## Suggested Fix\n\nDetect the merge commit and use \\`HEAD^2^..HEAD^2\\` to get the per-commit diff:\n\n\\`\\`\\`javascript\nfunction isMergeCommit() {\n  const parentCount = exec('git cat-file -p HEAD')\n    .split('\\n')\n    .filter((line) => line.startsWith('parent ')).length;\n  return parentCount > 1;\n}\n\nfunction getChangedFiles() {\n  if (isMergeCommit()) {\n    console.log('Merge commit detected (pull_request event)');\n    console.log('Comparing HEAD^2^ to HEAD^2 (per-commit diff of PR head)');\n    try {\n      const output = exec('git diff --name-only HEAD^2^ HEAD^2');\n      return output ? output.split('\\n').filter(Boolean) : [];\n    } catch {\n      // First commit in PR — fall back to full diff against base\n      const output = exec('git diff --name-only HEAD^ HEAD^2');\n      return output ? output.split('\\n').filter(Boolean) : [];\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Push events: HEAD is the real commit\n  console.log('Comparing HEAD^ to HEAD');\n  try {\n    const output = exec('git diff --name-only HEAD^ HEAD');\n    return output ? output.split('\\n').filter(Boolean) : [];\n  } catch {\n    const output = exec('git ls-tree --name-only -r HEAD');\n    return output ? output.split('\\n').filter(Boolean) : [];\n  }\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n### Workaround\n\nThe fix has been implemented and verified in CI in [link-assistant/web-capture PR #51](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/pull/51).\n\nRelated issue: https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/issues/50",
