+    "body": "## Summary\n\nIncorporates all proven CI/CD best practices from [link-assistant/hive-mind](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind) into this template repository, as requested in #29.\n\n### Gap Analysis & Changes\n\nAfter a comprehensive comparison of both repositories' CI/CD configurations, **7 gaps** were identified and addressed:\n\n| # | Gap | Solution |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | No test-compilation job | Added `scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh` + `test-compilation` job (~7s fast check) |\n| 2 | No file line limits CI check | Added `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` + `check-file-line-limits` job |\n| 3 | No fast-fail job ordering | Slow test matrix now gates on fast checks (test-compilation, lint, file-limits) |\n| 4 | Uses `always()` instead of `!cancelled()` | Fixed per hive-mind issue #1278 for proper cancellation propagation |\n| 5 | No secrets detection | Added `secretlint` step with `.secretlintrc.json` config |\n| 6 | No documentation validation | Added `validate-docs` job (file size limits + required files check) |\n| 7 | Inline fresh merge simulation | Extracted to reusable `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` |\n\n### Documentation Sync\n\nAll documentation has been verified and updated to accurately reflect the repository's actual CI/CD configuration:\n\n- **README.md**: Updated CI/CD Pipeline section to document all checks (test compilation, secrets scan, file line limits, documentation validation). Fixed file size limit from 1000 to 1500 lines.\n- **CONTRIBUTING.md**: Updated CI checks list to include all new checks. Fixed file size limit from 1000 to 1500 lines.\n- **BEST-PRACTICES.md**: Comprehensive documentation of all 13 practices with explanations of **why** each feature exists and **how** it is implemented.\n- **Case study (issue-29)**: Full gap analysis with before/after comparison and references.\n\n### New Files\n- `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` — Reusable fresh merge simulation\n- `scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh` — Node.js syntax check for all .mjs files\n- `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` — 1500-line limit enforcement\n- `.secretlintrc.json` — Secrets detection configuration\n- `docs/case-studies/issue-29/README.md` — Full case study with gap analysis\n\n### Updated Files\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml` — 5 new jobs/steps, fixed cancellation propagation\n- `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md` — 13 documented practices with detailed explanations\n- `README.md` — Updated CI/CD pipeline section and file size limit\n- `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` — Updated CI checks list and file size limit\n- `.changeset/ci-cd-best-practices.md` — Minor version bump changeset\n\n### CI Pipeline Structure (After)\n```\nFast checks (~7-30s):         Slow checks (~1-10 min):\n├── test-compilation          └── test matrix (3 runtimes × 3 OS)\n├── lint + secrets scan           ↑ gates on all fast checks\n├── check-file-line-limits\n├── version-check\n├── changeset-check\n└── validate-docs\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] All local tests pass (`npm test` — 6/6)\n- [x] ESLint passes (`npm run lint`)\n- [x] Prettier formatting passes (`npm run format:check`)\n- [x] Code duplication check passes (`npm run check:duplication`)\n- [x] New scripts work locally (`check-mjs-syntax.sh`, `check-file-line-limits.sh`)\n- [x] All documentation is in sync with repository content\n- [ ] CI workflow runs successfully on this PR\n\n## References\n- Source: [hive-mind CI/CD Best Practices](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md)\n- Case study: [docs/case-studies/issue-29/README.md](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/blob/issue-29-2f358775b13e/docs/case-studies/issue-29/README.md)\n\nCloses #29\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
