+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR incorporates best CI/CD practices from the [hive-mind repository](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind), specifically addressing the critical issue of **stale merge preview** in GitHub Actions.\n\n### Key Changes\n\n1. **Fresh Merge Simulation**: Added to both `lint` and `test` jobs in the CI workflow\n   - Fetches the latest base branch when running PR checks\n   - Merges it to simulate the actual merge result\n   - Prevents stale merge preview issues where PRs pass CI but fail after merge\n\n2. **Case Study Documentation**: Comprehensive analysis in `docs/case-studies/issue-23/`\n   - Root cause analysis of GitHub's merge preview architecture\n   - Timeline of events from hive-mind issue #1141\n   - Online research on best practices\n   - Raw data from referenced PRs for future reference\n\n3. **Configuration Updates**:\n   - Add ignore patterns for case study data files in ESLint and Prettier\n   - Update lint-staged to suppress warnings for ignored files\n\n### The Problem Being Solved\n\nWhen a PR triggers a GitHub Actions workflow, GitHub creates a synthetic merge commit at `refs/pull/{number}/merge`. This is a **snapshot** that does NOT automatically update when the base branch changes. This leads to:\n\n```\nDay 1: PR opened -> CI passes (validates against snapshot)\n[Time passes - other PRs merge to main]\nDay N: PR merged -> Main CI fails (actual merge differs from snapshot)\n```\n\n### The Solution\n\nThe fresh merge simulation step ensures PR CI validates the **actual** merge result:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Simulate fresh merge with base branch (PR only)\n  if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\n  run: |\n    git fetch origin \"$BASE_REF\"\n    BEHIND_COUNT=$(git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/$BASE_REF)\n    if [ \"$BEHIND_COUNT\" -gt 0 ]; then\n      git merge origin/$BASE_REF --no-edit || exit 1\n    fi\n```\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] `npm run lint` passes\n- [x] `npm run format:check` passes\n- [x] `npm run check:duplication` passes\n- [x] `npm test` passes\n- [x] Changeset added for versioning\n\n## References\n\n- [hive-mind Issue #1141](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1141): Make sure our lines count checks are synchronized in CI/CD\n- [hive-mind PR #1142](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/1142): fix: synchronize line count checks in CI/CD\n- [hive-mind PR #1127](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/1127): Add version-check CI job\n\nFixes #23\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
