+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR implements best practices for supporting both single-language and multi-language repository structures in CI/CD scripts, based on case study analysis of related issues in the link-assistant/agent repository.\n\n**Related Issues:**\n- [link-assistant/agent#111](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/111) - JS release does not work (npm ERESOLVE)\n- [link-assistant/agent#113](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/113) - JavaScript publish does not work (working directory corruption)\n- [link-assistant/agent PR #112](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/112) - fix: Add --legacy-peer-deps flag to release scripts\n- [link-assistant/agent PR #114](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/114) - feat: Add configurable package root for release scripts\n- [link-assistant/agent#115](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/115) - Error was treated as success\n- [link-assistant/agent PR #116](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/116) - fix: Add publish verification and failure detection to prevent false positives\n\n## Changes\n\n### New Utility Module\n- `scripts/js-paths.mjs` - JavaScript package root detection utility\n\n### Updated Scripts\n- `scripts/changeset-version.mjs`\n- `scripts/instant-version-bump.mjs`\n- `scripts/version-and-commit.mjs`\n- `scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs`\n\n### Case Study Documentation\n- `docs/case-studies/issue-21/` - Detailed root cause analysis with preserved CI logs\n\n### Test Scripts\n- `experiments/test-failure-detection.mjs` - Validates failure detection patterns\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. Automatic Package Root Detection\n- Checks for `./package.json` first (single-language repo)\n- Falls back to `./js/package.json` (multi-language repo)\n- Supports explicit configuration via:\n  - CLI: `--js-root <path>`\n  - Environment: `JS_ROOT=<path>`\n\n### 2. Fixed npm ERESOLVE Errors\n- Added `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to all `npm install --package-lock-only` commands\n- Ensures consistent behavior across workflow files and release scripts\n\n### 3. Fixed Working Directory Corruption\n- Save and restore `process.cwd()` after `cd` commands\n- The `command-stream` library's `cd` is a virtual command that calls `process.chdir()`, permanently changing the Node.js working directory\n\n### 4. Prevent False Positives in CI/CD (NEW - from PR #116)\nMulti-layer failure detection in `publish-to-npm.mjs`:\n- **Output pattern matching** for known error messages (`packages failed to publish`, `npm error code E`, etc.)\n- **Exit code checking** (when available)\n- **Post-publish verification** by querying npm registry\n\nThe `changeset publish` command exits with code 0 even when packages fail to publish. This is a known upstream issue ([changesets#1621](https://github.com/changesets/changesets/issues/1621), [changesets#1280](https://github.com/changesets/changesets/issues/1280)). Our multi-layer detection prevents false positive success reports.\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n```bash\n# Auto-detection (default for single-language repos)\nnode scripts/version-and-commit.mjs --mode changeset\n\n# Explicit configuration for multi-language repos\nnode scripts/version-and-commit.mjs --mode changeset --js-root js\n\n# Via environment variable\nJS_ROOT=js node scripts/version-and-commit.mjs --mode changeset\n```\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] Local lint and format checks pass\n- [x] All unit tests pass\n- [x] Failure detection test passes (`node experiments/test-failure-detection.mjs`)\n- [ ] CI workflow passes on this PR\n\nFixes #21\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
