+    "body": "## Investigation Summary\n\nThis PR was created to apply changes from [hive-mind PR #957](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/957) to ensure package-lock.json is synchronized during version bumps.\n\n### Findings\n\n✅ **The fix is already implemented** - No changes needed.\n\nThis repository was created with the package-lock.json synchronization feature already in place since the initial commit (0f9c0db). Both release modes properly synchronize package-lock.json after version bumps.\n\n### Evidence\n\nThe fix from PR #957 involved adding `npm install --package-lock-only` after running changeset version. This is already implemented in both release modes:\n\n**1. Changeset Mode** (scripts/changeset-version.mjs:28-29):\n```javascript\nconsole.log('\\nSynchronizing package-lock.json...');\nawait $`npm install --package-lock-only`;\n```\n\n**2. Instant Release Mode** (scripts/instant-version-bump.mjs:109-111):\n```javascript\nconsole.log('\\nSynchronizing package-lock.json...');\nawait $`npm install --package-lock-only`;\n```\n\n### How It Works\n\nWhen a version bump occurs:\n1. The version is updated in package.json\n2. The CHANGELOG is updated\n3. **npm install --package-lock-only** is run to sync package-lock.json\n4. All changes (package.json, package-lock.json, CHANGELOG.md) are committed together\n\nThis ensures package-lock.json always reflects the correct version, preventing the issue that was fixed in hive-mind PR #957.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nThis PR can be closed as the requested functionality is already implemented and working correctly.\n\n---\n\nFixes #11",
