+    "body": "## What\n\n- Route pull-request branch names and manual release inputs through step environment variables before shell use.\n- Add a workflow-wide regression scan that rejects contributor-controlled expressions in every `run:` block.\n- Configure `init.defaultBranch=main` before checkout in all workflows.\n- Move concurrency from workflow scope to job scope: stale read-only jobs cancel independently, while Pages, preview generation, npm releases, Docker publishing, and changeset PR creation share one non-cancelling writer queue.\n- Default the example-app workflow token to read-only and escalate permissions only on deploy/write jobs.\n- Document cancellation, dependency, active-writer, and matrix edge cases.\n- Add a patch changeset.\n\n## Why\n\nGitHub expands expressions before the shell parses a `run:` command. A fork branch name or free-form workflow-dispatch description could therefore become executable shell syntax. Workflow-level cancellation also cannot save CI minutes on read-only `main` checks without risking interruption of an already-running publisher.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nBefore the workflow changes, the new focused tests failed because:\n\n1. `changeset-check` interpolated `github.head_ref` directly into Bash.\n2. Both manual release paths interpolated free-form dispatch values directly into commands.\n3. `example-app.yml` and `links.yml` lacked checkout-time default-branch configuration.\n4. Workflows used run-level concurrency, and several write/deploy jobs lacked the shared protected writer group.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test` — 196 passing\n- `bun test --timeout 30000` — 196 passing\n- `deno test --allow-read` — 165 passing\n- `npm run check`\n- `bash scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`\n- `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n- `GITHUB_BASE_REF=main node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`\n- Parsed all workflow YAML files successfully\n\nFixes #115",
