+    "body": "Fixes #87\n\n## What\n\n- Make `scripts/merge-changesets.mjs` fail fast when any pending changeset cannot be parsed, instead of warning and skipping it.\n- Emit a GitHub Actions `::error::` on merge-time parse failures so release CI fails visibly.\n- Tighten the shared changeset bump regex so values like `patches` no longer match `patch`.\n- Add regression coverage for the malformed-changeset merge path and the exact bump-token parser.\n- Add a patch changeset for the fix.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe new `tests/merge-changesets.test.js` fixture creates two pending changesets: one valid file and one malformed file using `patches` as the bump value. Before the fix, merge exited `0`, merged the valid file, and left the malformed note out of the release flow. After the fix, merge exits nonzero and leaves both source files untouched.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/package-info.test.js tests/merge-changesets.test.js`\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `bun test --timeout 30000`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- GitHub Actions passed for `e7356e9`: Broken Link Checker and Checks and release, including Node/Bun/Deno matrices on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows.\n",
