+    "body": "## Summary\n\n- adopts `@link-foundation/example-package-name` as the real scoped package name, with public publish metadata, a changeset, and a packed runtime file list\n- adds the globally installable `example-package-name` CLI and regression coverage for direct and npm-bin-link invocation\n- fixes the GitHub Pages deployment path by adding Pages permissions plus `actions/configure-pages@v6`, and enables repository Pages for workflow deployments\n- stores the issue 58 investigation, failed CI logs, template comparison data, registry probes, and local verification logs under `docs/case-studies/issue-58/`\n\n## Reproduction / Root Cause\n\n- `Checks and release` run `25733140225` failed after PR 57 because the release still targeted `my-package@0.10.0`; npm returned `404 Not Found - PUT https://registry.npmjs.org/my-package`.\n- `Example app` run `25733140224` built and uploaded web plus desktop artifacts, then failed at `actions/deploy-pages@v5` with status 404 because GitHub Pages was not enabled for the repository.\n- Temporary global install testing exposed a CLI entrypoint edge case through npm bin links; the CLI now resolves real paths before deciding whether to execute.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/*.test.js`\n- `bun test --timeout 30000`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- `npm run check`\n- `npx --yes -p secretlint -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend secretlint \"**/*\"`\n- `bash scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`\n- `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n- `node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`\n- `npm pack --dry-run --json --ignore-scripts`\n- `npm install -g . --prefix /tmp/issue-58-global-prefix && /tmp/issue-58-global-prefix/bin/example-package-name multiply 6 7`\n- `npm run example:web:build`\n- `npm run example:desktop:package`\n- `npm run example:mobile:sync`\n\n## Notes\n\nThe local checkout is not authenticated to npm, so npm-side trusted publisher setup could not be completed from this machine. The release workflow keeps the required OIDC `id-token: write` permissions and npm registry configuration; the first main release still requires npm trusted publishing to be configured for `@link-foundation/example-package-name` and this repository workflow.\n\nCloses #58",
