+    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Enforce Node.js >= 22.14.0 and npm >= 11.5.1 for the trusted publishing setup path.\n- Resolve the latest supported npm 11.x tarball from npm registry metadata for the curl fallback instead of using the old 11.4.2 tarball.\n- Re-check the final npm version after all setup strategies and fail if it still does not satisfy the trusted publishing minimum.\n- Add regression coverage for numeric version comparison, npm minimum enforcement, Node minimum enforcement, and fallback tarball selection.\n- Remove the automated `.gitkeep` placeholder from the PR branch.\n\nFixes #48\n\n## Reproduction Covered\n\nThe previous script could accept npm 11.4.2 because it checked only the major version after fallback failures, and its curl fallback was pinned to npm 11.4.2. The new `tests/setup-npm.test.js` verifies that 11.4.2 and 11.5.0 are rejected, 11.5.1+ is accepted, and the fallback selector ignores unsupported npm 11 versions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `bash scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`\n- `node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`\n- `bun test --timeout 30000`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- `node scripts/setup-npm.mjs` under local Node.js v20.20.2 exits with the expected Node.js >= 22.14.0 error\n- GitHub Actions for head `06572bad4376a865a704fef5241d84a855fd5ddc`: `Checks and release` passed, `Broken Link Checker` passed\n",
