+    "body": "Fixes #41.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds a `WARN_THRESHOLD=1350` warn band to `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh` for checked `.mjs` files and `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n- Keeps the existing hard failure unchanged for files over 1500 lines.\n- Emits GitHub Actions `::warning` annotations and a non-blocking warning summary for near-limit files.\n- Normalizes padded `wc -l` output so warning and error lines are stable across GNU and BSD environments.\n- Adds `tests/check-file-line-limits.test.js`, including fixtures for 1351-line warnings and 1501-line failures.\n- Preserves the investigation, downloaded issue data, CI logs, and template comparisons under `docs/case-studies/issue-41`.\n- Filed the sibling Rust template report: https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/40\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe new test was written before the script change. Against the previous script it failed because `WARN_THRESHOLD=1350` was missing and a 1351-line `.mjs` file passed silently. With this PR, the same fixture exits 0 with warnings, while a 1501-line file still exits 1.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n- `bash scripts/check-mjs-syntax.sh`\n- `bun test`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- `npx --yes -p secretlint -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend secretlint \"**/*\"`\n- `GITHUB_BASE_REF=main node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`\n- Documentation file-size validation for `docs/**/*.md`\n\n## Research Notes\n\nThe case study captures the downstream `hive-mind` incidents, failed CI logs, relevant workflow/script snapshots, and the Rust template comparison. Online references used for the implementation notes:\n\n- GitHub Actions workflow command annotations: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-workflows/workflow-commands-for-github-actions\n- ESLint `max-lines`: https://eslint.org/docs/latest/rules/max-lines\n\n",
