+    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements best practices from the [hive-mind](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind) repository as requested in issue #25. This PR provides a **comprehensive analysis of ALL scripts, workflows, and configurations** in both repositories.\n\n### What was done:\n\n- **Added `docs/case-studies/issue-25/DETAILED-COMPARISON.md`** - Complete side-by-side comparison of:\n  - All 15+ scripts in both repositories\n  - GitHub Actions workflow structure and jobs\n  - ESLint configurations and rules\n  - Package.json scripts and dependencies\n  - Configuration files comparison\n- **Updated `docs/BEST-PRACTICES.md`** - Fixed max-lines value (1500, not 1000), added reference to detailed comparison\n- **Implemented `cancel-in-progress` concurrency** - Applied hive-mind Issue #1274 fix to prevent workflow blocking\n- **Created `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`** - Detailed contribution guidelines including changeset workflow\n- **Created `docs/case-studies/issue-25/`** - Full case study analysis with supporting data\n\n### Key Findings\n\nThe analysis revealed that this template **already implements most critical CI/CD best practices** from hive-mind:\n\n| Best Practice | Status |\n|---------------|--------|\n| Concurrency with cancel-in-progress | ✅ Implemented (this PR) |\n| Fresh merge simulation | ✅ Implemented |\n| Multi-runtime testing (Node.js, Bun, Deno) | ✅ Implemented |\n| Cross-platform testing (Ubuntu, macOS, Windows) | ✅ Implemented |\n| OIDC trusted publishing | ✅ Implemented |\n| Changeset-based versioning | ✅ Implemented |\n| ESLint max-lines rule | ✅ Implemented |\n| Code duplication check | ✅ Implemented |\n\n### Features This Template Has That hive-mind Doesn't\n\n| Feature | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| Code duplication detection (jscpd) | Catches copy-paste issues |\n| Deno runtime support | Multi-runtime flexibility |\n| TypeScript declarations | Better IDE support |\n| Comprehensive ESLint rules | Complexity, depth, params limits |\n| Combined `npm run check` script | Simplified local validation |\n| 3x3 test matrix | 3 runtimes x 3 platforms |\n\n### Features hive-mind Has That Are Not Applicable Here\n\n| Feature | Reason |\n|---------|--------|\n| Docker multi-arch builds | Template has no Docker |\n| Helm chart automation | Template has no Kubernetes deployment |\n| Sentry source map upload | Template doesn't use Sentry |\n| Custom `gh api` ESLint rule | Template doesn't heavily use GitHub API |\n\n### Referenced Issues Analysis\n\n- **Issue #1274**: Analyzed concurrency blocking due to slow ARM64 Docker builds - **fix applied** (`cancel-in-progress`)\n- **Issue #1278**: Analyzed `always()` vs `!cancelled()` issue - not applicable (no Docker jobs in this template)\n\n### Reverse Issue Created\n\nCreated [hive-mind#1286](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/1286) to document best practices this template has that hive-mind could adopt:\n- Multi-runtime testing (Bun, Deno support)\n- Code duplication detection (`.jscpd.json`)\n- TypeScript declaration files\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] Run `npm run check` locally (lint, format, duplication check)\n- [x] Verify new documentation files are properly formatted\n- [x] Verify case study data files are complete\n- [ ] CI/CD pipeline passes all checks\n\n## Fixes\n\nFixes #25\n\n---\nGenerated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/claude-code)",
