+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR adds ESLint complexity checks with reasonable thresholds that encourage code maintainability without being overly strict, addressing the concern from #8 that the strict 50 lines per function limit was too restrictive.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nAdded the following ESLint complexity rules to `eslint.config.js`:\n\n### Complexity Rules Added\n\n| Rule | Threshold | Comparison | Rationale |\n|------|-----------|------------|-----------|\n| **complexity** | 15 | vs strict 8 | Allows moderately complex logic when needed |\n| **max-depth** | 5 | vs strict 4 | Permits slightly deeper nesting for real-world scenarios |\n| **max-lines-per-function** | 150 | vs strict 50 | More reasonable for orchestration and coordination functions |\n| **max-params** | 6 | vs strict 5 | Allows additional parameters when justified |\n| **max-statements** | 60 | vs strict 30 | Accommodates longer orchestration functions |\n| **max-lines** | 1500 per file | vs strict 300 | Total line count including blank lines and comments |\n\n### Configuration Details\n\nAll rules are configured at the **'warn'** level (not 'error') to:\n- Provide helpful feedback to developers\n- Highlight potential refactoring opportunities\n- Avoid blocking development or causing CI failures\n- Encourage but not enforce code quality improvements\n\nFor `max-lines-per-function`:\n- `skipBlankLines: true` - blank lines don't count toward function limits\n- `skipComments: true` - comment lines don't count toward function limits\n\nFor `max-lines`:\n- Counts **all lines** including blank lines and comments (no skip options)\n- The 1500 limit is the total physical line count of the file\n\nThis ensures that:\n- Well-documented functions aren't penalized by documentation overhead\n- File size limits are strict and count everything to maintain reasonable file sizes\n\n## Testing\n\n✅ All existing code passes the new complexity checks\n✅ Local CI checks pass (`npm run check`)\n✅ ESLint runs without errors or warnings\n✅ Pre-commit hooks pass successfully\n\n## References\n\n- Fixes #9\n- Related to #8 (effect-template best practices analysis)\n\n## Comparison with effect-template\n\nThe effect-template repository uses very strict limits:\n- 8 cyclomatic complexity\n- 50 lines per function\n- 4 max nesting depth\n\nOur more lenient values (15, 150, 5 respectively) provide a better balance for this project while still encouraging maintainable code.\n\n---\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
