+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR provides a comprehensive analysis of best practices from [ProverCoderAI/effect-template](https://github.com/ProverCoderAI/effect-template) compared to our repository, as requested in #7.\n\n### Documentation Added\n\nAll analysis data and findings are documented in `./docs/case-studies/issue-7/`:\n\n- **BEST-PRACTICES-COMPARISON.md** - Detailed comparison with recommendations\n- **FORMATTER-COMPARISON.md** - NEW: Comprehensive formatter comparison (Prettier, Biome, dprint, Standard JS)\n- **effect-template-analysis.json** - Raw data extracted from effect-template\n- **current-repository-analysis.json** - Our repository's current state\n\n### Implementations Added\n\n✅ **Code Duplication Detection (jscpd)**\n- Added `.jscpd.json` configuration\n- Integrated into CI workflow and `npm run check`\n- Reports saved to `reports/` directory (gitignored)\n\n### Formatter Comparison Analysis\n\nAdded comprehensive analysis of JavaScript/TypeScript formatters for 2025:\n\n| Formatter | Speed vs Prettier | Best For |\n|-----------|------------------|----------|\n| **Prettier** | 1x (baseline) | Industry standard, multi-language support |\n| **Biome** | 7-100x faster | All-in-one linter+formatter, TypeScript projects |\n| **dprint** | 20-60x faster | Specialized formatting, minimal dependencies |\n| **Standard JS** | ~1x | Zero-config, small projects |\n\n**Key Findings:**\n- All formatters support CI checks, pre-commit hooks, and autoformatting\n- Biome is gaining rapid adoption in 2025 (80% faster build pipelines)\n- Our current Prettier + ESLint setup remains solid and stable\n- See `FORMATTER-COMPARISON.md` for detailed migration considerations\n\n### Key Findings\n\n#### Best Practices Missing in Our Repository\n\n**High Priority (Recommended to Add):**\n1. ✅ **Code duplication detection** - IMPLEMENTED (jscpd configuration)\n2. **ESLint complexity rules** - Add max-complexity, max-lines-per-function, max-params\n3. **VS Code settings** - Add .vscode/settings.json for team consistency\n4. **Reusable GitHub Action** - Extract setup steps to custom action\n\n**Medium Priority (Consider Adding):**\n5. **Test coverage thresholds** - Add coverage configuration with minimum thresholds\n6. **Type checking script** - Add `npm run typecheck` if using TypeScript\n7. **Package snapshots** - Add pkg-pr-new for PR testing\n\n**Lower Priority (Optional):**\n8. **TypeScript migration** - Full TypeScript with strict config\n9. **Vite build tool** - For TypeScript compilation\n10. **Nix environment** - For reproducible development\n\n### Comparison Summary\n\n| Category | effect-template | Our Repository | Status |\n|----------|-----------------|----------------|--------|\n| TypeScript Support | Full TypeScript with strict config | JavaScript with .d.ts | Different approach |\n| Build Tool | Vite | None (direct execution) | Missing |\n| Test Framework | Vitest with coverage | test-anywhere | Different approach |\n| Code Duplication | jscpd | ✅ **ADDED** | **Implemented** |\n| Linting | ESLint + Biome | ESLint + Prettier | Present |\n| Complexity Rules | Yes (max 8 complexity, 50 lines/fn) | None | **Missing** |\n| Coverage Thresholds | 100% for core | None | **Missing** |\n| VS Code Config | Comprehensive | None | **Missing** |\n| Custom GH Actions | Setup action | Inline setup | **Missing** |\n\n### References\n\n- [jscpd - Copy/paste detector](https://github.com/kucherenko/jscpd)\n- [Biome - Toolchain of the web](https://biomejs.dev/)\n- [dprint - Fast formatter](https://dprint.dev/)\n- [Vitest Coverage Guide](https://vitest.dev/guide/coverage)\n- [ESLint Complexity Rules](https://eslint.org/docs/rules/complexity)\n\n---\n\nFixes #7\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
