+    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR implements a strict `no-unused-vars` ESLint rule without any exceptions, as requested in issue #5.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **ESLint Configuration** (`eslint.config.js:35`)\n   - Removed all ignore patterns from the `no-unused-vars` rule\n   - Changed from complex object configuration to simple `'error'` setting\n   - No more exceptions for `_` prefix variables, arguments, or caught errors\n\n2. **Documentation** (`README.md:147`)\n   - Added explicit documentation about the strict unused variables rule\n   - Clearly states that no exceptions are allowed (no `_` prefix exceptions)\n\n3. **Code Fix** (`scripts/publish-to-npm.mjs:111-114`)\n   - Fixed unused `_error` variable in retry logic\n   - Now logs error message during retry attempts for better debugging\n   - Changed from `catch (_error)` to `catch (error)` with proper usage\n\n### Testing\n\n- ✅ All ESLint checks pass with zero warnings\n- ✅ All tests pass (6/6)\n- ✅ Code formatting verified with Prettier\n- ✅ File size limits respected\n- ✅ Pre-commit hooks executed successfully\n\n### Design Rationale\n\nThe strict `no-unused-vars` rule without exceptions enforces cleaner code by:\n- Eliminating dead code and unused variables completely\n- Preventing the common pattern of \"ignoring\" variables with `_` prefix\n- Making developers explicitly remove or use all declared variables\n- Improving code maintainability and readability\n\nFixes #5\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
